                %em Synthetic 1-Categories in Directed Type Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.19520"}> arXiv:2410.19520
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesCisinskiEtAl Cisinski et al.
          %ul
            %li#CisinskiEtAl23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hoang+Kim+Nguyen"} Hoang Kim Nguyen
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tashi+Walde"} Tashi Walde
              = succeed "," do
                %em Univalent Directed Type Theory
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/index.html"} CMU Homotopy Type Theory Seminar
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/previous.html#:~:text=Univalent%20Directed%20Type%20Theory"}> 13, 20, 27 Mar 2023
              ) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/index.html#230313"}> web
              , video 1:
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5YOltuTcBK8"}> YT
              , 2:
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xWmELBvHMPo"}> YT
              , 3:
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P0Cfb4eUJo4"}> YT
              ; slides 0:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-intro_talk1.pdf"}> pdf
              , 1:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk1.pdf"}> pdf
              , 2:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk2.pdf"}> pdf
              , 3:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk3.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %strong Abstract:
                  We will introduce a version of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
                  that is suitable to develop a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+mathematics"} synthetic
                  theory of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
                  are both a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fragment"} fragment
                  and an extension of ordinary
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
                  are chosen so that
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
                  (in the form of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
                  or
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+spaces"} complete Segal spaces
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} semantic interpretation
                  = succeed "\u2018s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Voevodsky
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalent
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory#Shulman19"} Shulman’s methods
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)‑categories internally
                  in any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} ∞‑topos
                  (as
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "internal+infinity1-category#ReferencesInternalToInfinityTopos"} developed by Martini and Wolf
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} semantic interpretation
                  as well (hence so is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Parametrized+Higher+Category+Theory+and+Higher+Algebra"} parametrized higher category theory
                  introduced by Barwick, Dotto, Glasman, Nardin and Shah). There are of course strong links with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-cosmoi"} ∞-cosmoi
                  of Riehl and Verity as well as with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical HoTT
                  (as strongly suggested by the work of Licata and Weaver), or
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+type+theory"} simplicial HoTT
                  (as in the work of Buchholtz and Weinberger). We will explain the axioms in detail and have a glimpse at basic theorems and constructions in this context (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+lemma"}> Yoneda Lemma
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Kan+extension"} Kan extensions
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} Localizations
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
                  natively (e.g. we can produce a logic by rectifying the idea of having a locally cartesian type). In particular, this logic can be used to produce and study
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} semantic interpretations
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT"} HoTT
          %p
            This is based on the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/straightening+and+unstraightening"} straightening and unstraightening
            entirely within the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            from
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hoang+Kim+Nguyen"} Hoang Kim Nguyen
              %em The universal coCartesian fibration
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.08945"}> arXiv:2210.08945
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            which (along the lines of the discussion of the universal left fibration from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "universal+left+fibration#Cisinski19"} Cisinski 2019
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coCartesian+fibration"} universal coCartesian fibration
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+homotopy+type+theory"} directed homotopy type theory
            (see
            %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/P0Cfb4eUJo4?t=4618"} video 3 at 1:16:58
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk3.pdf#page=33"} slide 3.33
          %p#CisinskiOnSyntax
            But the actual type-theoretic syntax (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"}> inference rules
            ) for this intended semantics remains to be given:
          %blockquote
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"} Cisinski
              in
              = succeed "&rbrack;:" do
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/P0Cfb4eUJo4?t=5263"} video 3 at 1:27:43
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
              yet and actually I would be very happy to discuss that, because we don’t know yet and I have questions myself, actually.
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"} Awodey
              in
              = succeed "&rbrack;:" do
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/P0Cfb4eUJo4?t=6383"} video 3 at 1:46:23
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lambda-calculus"} lambda-calculus
            %p Some people would prefer to call a type theory only something which can immediately be implemented in a computer. So that’s different than an abstract description of a structure that we would want to describe in such a type theory.
          %blockquote
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"} Cisinski
              in
              = succeed "&rbrack;:" do
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/P0Cfb4eUJo4?t=6568"} video 3 at 1:49:28
          %p
            More on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+univalence+axiom"} directed univalence axiom
            in this context:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hoang+Kim+Nguyen"}> Hoang Kim Nguyen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Directed univalence in simplicial sets
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/kapulkin/seminars/hottest.html"} Homotopy Type Theory Electronic Seminar Talks
              (March 2023) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GgcJqzGvq80"}> video
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/kapulkin/seminars/hottestfiles/Nguyen-2023-03-09-HoTTEST.pdf"} slides
          %p A monograph in preparation:
          %ul
            %li#CCNW25
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bastiaan+Cnossen"} Bastiaan Cnossen
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hoang+Kim+Nguyen"} Hoang Kim Nguyen
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tashi+Walde"} Tashi Walde
              = succeed "," do
                %em Formalization of Higher Categories
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lKaq7watGGl3xvjqw9qHjm6SDPFJ2-0o/view"} pdf
